      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Marks presents \"homeostatic theory\" which proposes that weight gain is fostered by a \"Circle of Discontent\" consisting of body dissatisfaction, negative affect, and overconsumption. This innovative framework offers potential intervention approaches, including victim-blaming, stigma, and discrimination, as well as devalorizing the thin-ideal. Our article discusses possible ways that clinical health psychologists based in university settings may be uniquely positioned to consider and implement large-scale programs that have shown great promise for addressing these core issues."},
